 "nan_confounder": {
  "fact": "the four OOF stack columns are NaN on exactly the earliest season of each training pool: 24.304% of fold_2023's pool (211,627 of 870,752 = every 2019 row), 18.958% of fold_2024's, 32.372% of block 2022's.",
  "identical_in_the_control": "exp_020 B3_exp016_path.fold_2023 and every exp_024 blocks/*.json record the SAME percentages (24.304 / 18.958 / 32.372), so the NaN FRACTION is not a variable between the arms.",
  "catboost_nan_mode": "Min (catboost 1.2.10 default, confirmed by get_all_params() on a probe fit with this exact CB_BASE) \u2014 NaN is replaced by a value below the feature's minimum, a fixed rule.",
  "lightgbm_nan_handling": "learned default direction per split.",
  "why_it_is_bounded_here": "within any training pool the NaN set is EXACTLY {season == earliest season}, and `season` is itself one of the 47 features. Both families can therefore isolate the NaN group exactly with a single split on season, so the difference cannot be about identifying the group \u2014 only about where the imputed value lands inside an already-separable region. No sentinel fill was used and no missing-flag column was added (it would be collinear with season).",
  "honest_label": "the headline delta is nevertheless reported as the effect of 'the CatBoost C5 configuration including its native NaN handling', not of the model family alone. No arm isolating nan_mode was run."
 },
